From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:45:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 182/182] fix(gastown): pin mol-polecat-work steps to one
 continuation group (gcp-fm79v)

A polecat that closed a step and ran gc hook --claim for the next one could be
handed an older, higher-priority routed pool bead from another molecule instead
of its own ready step (winnow-xd06q4: nux took winnow-w6k.4 while its own
submit-and-exit step sat open and unassigned).

Root cause: gascity #5622 (c91381b22) stopped stamping a blanket
gc.continuation_group on pool-routed graph steps. Continuation is now
formula-declared only, and mol-polecat-work declared none, so its steps stayed
plain pool work, sorted by priority then created_at.

Declare gc.continuation_group = "main" and gc.session_affinity = "require" on
the four steps this formula defines (workspace-setup, preflight-tests,
self-review, submit-and-exit), matching core's mol-scoped-work. A child step
replaces its parent's wholesale, so the pack's overriding steps must carry the
declaration themselves. The first claim of a grouped step then pins its grouped
siblings to the claiming session and the continuation claim returns them as
ready_assignment. Affinity is advisory, so a dead session's pinned steps still
return to the open pool.

load-context and implement live only in gc core's mol-polecat-base and stay
unpinned until gcp-w4t8r lands the base-side half.

tests/test_polecat_continuation_group.py pins the declaration in the TOML and,
with GC_TEST_BIN set, in the workflow gc compiles from it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
